From: Cheap Phone OS stage-0 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] debug: avoid zero-length format in sysdump tail marker

The pinned SharkL3 donor builds with -Werror=format-zero-length under the
donor-era AOSP GCC 4.9 toolchain. The tail marker only needs an empty C
string, so terminate it directly instead of calling sprintf with an empty
format.

--- a/drivers/soc/sprd/debug/sysdump/sysdump.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sprd/debug/sysdump/sysdump.c
@@ -1221,7 +1221,7 @@ int minidump_save_extend_information(const char *name,
 			name, paddr_start, paddr_end);
 
 	tail_section = &minidump_info_g.section_info_total.section_info[section_tail];
-	sprintf(tail_section->section_name, "");
+	tail_section->section_name[0] = '\0';
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(minidump_save_extend_information);
